WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.934
-Welcome, everybody.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:03.934 --> 00:00:06.634
You're here. You made it.
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:10.567
Guys, today is December 1st,
which means it's time

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:12.267
to play that
classic December game,

00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:14.567
"Can you finish your lunch
before the sun goes down?"

00:00:14.567 --> 00:00:17.300
Yeah, that's right.
It's December 1st.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.234
The holiday season is here.

00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:21.567
I hate to be old-fashioned,
but does anyone else think

00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:23.367
Christmas has taken
all the meaning away from

00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:26.167
the Lexus December to Remember?

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:29.901
You can tell it's the
holiday season in New York City.

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:32.400
This morning, I told my Uber
driver, "Rockefeller Center,"

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.167
and he just abandoned his car
and never came back.

00:00:37.901 --> 00:00:39.334
Yep, now that
the Rockefeller Center

00:00:39.334 --> 00:00:41.868
Christmas tree is up,
there are tourists everywhere.

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:43.868
And now that weed
is legal in New York,

00:00:43.868 --> 00:00:45.934
I kind of understand
staring at it for an hour.

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:47.234
I go...

00:00:50.601 --> 00:00:52.801
Well, it seems like there's
so much going on right now.

00:00:52.801 --> 00:00:55.567
Last night was the Rockefeller
Center Christmas tree got lit.

00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:57.400
The World Cup --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:00.200
The World Cup is in full swing.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.801
There's a new trailer for the
"Super Mario Bros. Movie."

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:04.934
-Ooh!
-That looks good.

00:01:04.934 --> 00:01:06.400
And Subway just announced that

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.868
they're going to sell
a foot-long cookie.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.334
There's a lot to go over,

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:12.200
so let's just jump in
and cover it all at once.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.834
It's time for a "News Smash."

00:01:13.834 --> 00:01:15.834
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:18.801 --> 00:01:21.100
First up, the Rockefeller Center
Christmas tree.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.434
Last night was the big lighting.

00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:24.501
Thousands of people
waited around for hours

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:26.467
just for one second
of excitement.

00:01:26.467 --> 00:01:28.934
Yeah, it was
just like watching...

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:30.133
the World Cup.

00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:31.767
Yeah.

00:01:31.767 --> 00:01:34.267
Games are long,
sometimes there's a tie,

00:01:34.267 --> 00:01:37.367
and the fans in Qatar
aren't even allowed to drink.

00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:39.434
But it hasn't stopped them
from enjoying the matches,

00:01:39.434 --> 00:01:41.834
which are full of
running, jumping, and kicking,

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:42.834
kind of like...

00:01:42.834 --> 00:01:44.501
"Super Mario."

00:01:44.501 --> 00:01:46.400
The new trailer for
the movie just came out.

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.701
Yeah, it's a whole movie
about a plumber,

00:01:48.701 --> 00:01:51.634
which is exactly who you'll
be calling if you eat a...

00:01:51.634 --> 00:01:54.167
foot-long cookie from Subway.

00:01:54.167 --> 00:01:57.267
That's right --
a giant 12-inch-long cookie.

00:01:57.267 --> 00:01:59.467
They're selling them
for National Cookie Day

00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:01.400
or, as stoners call it...

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:02.434
Christmas.

00:02:02.434 --> 00:02:05.567
The tree is so beautiful
when it's lit.

00:02:05.567 --> 00:02:07.567
But you know
who isn't lit right now?

00:02:07.567 --> 00:02:10.834
Fans at the World Cup.
There's no booze.

00:02:10.834 --> 00:02:13.634
But they still went wild when
Team USA's best player scored

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:15.801
while getting kneed
in the groin.

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:17.534
Yeah, he took one
right in his...

00:02:17.534 --> 00:02:18.801
cookies.

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:21.100
Seriously, if there's --
If you eat this whole thing,

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:22.701
you won't be hitting your
weight-loss...

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:25.567
goooooal!

00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:27.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.801
There are 16 countries left,

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:34.234
but there can only be
one winner.

00:02:34.234 --> 00:02:36.167
Right now,
every country is hoping...

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:37.534
"it's a-me."

00:02:37.534 --> 00:02:39.400
So, in conclusion...

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:40.868
what a star...

00:02:40.868 --> 00:02:42.067
in Qatar...

00:02:42.067 --> 00:02:43.534
"Super Mar"...

00:02:43.534 --> 00:02:44.834
you took it too far.

00:02:44.834 --> 00:02:46.667
This has been a "News Smash."

00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:48.667
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:50.834 --> 00:02:53.801
Oh, thank you very much.
Thank you.

00:02:53.801 --> 00:02:55.667
Well, here's some big news.

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:59.033
Today, President Biden hosted
French President Emmanuel Macron

00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:02.534
for the first White House state
dinner in more than three years.

00:03:02.534 --> 00:03:04.367
Yep, the French like
to eat late,

00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:05.400
so Biden was like, "Got it.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:08.067
4:30 it is."

00:03:08.067 --> 00:03:09.701
Can we see
Biden and Macron together?

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:10.934
Oh, yeah.

00:03:10.934 --> 00:03:13.901
Yeah, they look like
a father-and-son law firm.

00:03:13.901 --> 00:03:16.634
Tonight, Biden was --
It was the very first

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:18.868
White House state dinner
with Emmanuel Macron.

00:03:18.868 --> 00:03:20.501
Now, state dinners
are always very fancy

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:22.100
with lots of dishes and courses.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.267
So, just out of curiosity,
let's see if I can read

00:03:24.267 --> 00:03:27.601
the entire menu in less time
than it took Macron to break

00:03:27.601 --> 00:03:29.667
away from a handshake
with Donald Trump.

00:03:29.667 --> 00:03:31.667
Here we go. Let's try it.

00:03:31.667 --> 00:03:33.934
And let's run the handshake.

00:03:33.934 --> 00:03:35.501
Here we go.

00:03:35.501 --> 00:03:38.100
Butter-poached Maine lobster.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:40.267
American caviar.

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:44.067
Squash raviolo
with tarragon sauce.

00:03:44.067 --> 00:03:46.934
Beef with shallot marmalade.
That sounds good.

00:03:46.934 --> 00:03:49.434
Triple-cooked butter potatoes.

00:03:49.434 --> 00:03:51.901
Sunchoke-cream-watercress
red-wine reduction.

00:03:51.901 --> 00:03:53.868
Three artisanal cheeses.

00:03:53.868 --> 00:03:55.167
Orange chiffon cake.

00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:56.734
And roasted pears and ice cream.

00:03:56.734 --> 00:03:59.234
There you go.
That's a good menu.

00:03:59.234 --> 00:04:00.400
We did it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:04.501
♪♪

00:04:04.501 --> 00:04:06.501
-[ As Trump ] Oh!

00:04:07.767 --> 00:04:09.501
-[ As Trump ]
♪ Ring around the rosie ♪

00:04:09.501 --> 00:04:11.701
♪ Pocket -- ♪
[ Normal voice ] No.

00:04:11.701 --> 00:04:13.801
Meanwhile, last night,
the Bidens and the Macrons

00:04:13.801 --> 00:04:15.767
went out to dinner
at an Italian restaurant.

00:04:15.767 --> 00:04:16.901
-Ooh!
-Yeah.

00:04:16.901 --> 00:04:18.133
Here's a photo of
the two couples at dinner.

00:04:18.133 --> 00:04:19.434
There they are.

00:04:19.434 --> 00:04:21.467
Yep, the Bidens and Macrons
went on a double date.

00:04:21.467 --> 00:04:23.834
Then Kamala and Doug
showed up at the restaurant

00:04:23.834 --> 00:04:24.934
and pretended
it was an accident.

00:04:24.934 --> 00:04:26.367
"Oh, my gosh!

00:04:26.367 --> 00:04:28.234
You eat at the same...

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:30.634
I guess we should
just eat together, right?"

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:31.767
Switching gears.

00:04:31.767 --> 00:04:33.601
Well, guys, Prince William
and Princess Kate

00:04:33.601 --> 00:04:35.334
are on a trip in Boston.

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:37.701
And last night, they went to
a Boston Celtics game.

00:04:37.701 --> 00:04:39.634
And there's a photo going around
that really made me laugh.

00:04:39.634 --> 00:04:40.868
Can we see this photo?

00:04:44.067 --> 00:04:46.734
The photo already inspired
that new meme...

00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:54.634
Did you guys hear about this?

00:04:54.634 --> 00:04:56.734
There's a new study
from scientists in California

00:04:56.734 --> 00:05:00.434
that found that
eating foods with a high --

00:05:00.434 --> 00:05:02.033
-Jimmy!
-Wait, wait.

00:05:02.033 --> 00:05:04.167
-Jimmy,
I thought we were friends.

00:05:04.167 --> 00:05:07.067
-Wait. Keke.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:09.434 --> 00:05:10.567
Keke Palmer!

00:05:10.567 --> 00:05:11.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:05:11.634 --> 00:05:14.634
Keke Palmer. Keke Palmer?

00:05:14.634 --> 00:05:15.834
-Jimmy...
-What?

00:05:15.834 --> 00:05:18.367
-...I said,
"I thought we were friends."

00:05:18.367 --> 00:05:20.234
-No, we are friends.
Of course, we're friends.

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:22.200
-Well, then why didn't
you say that I'm hosting

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:25.567
"SNL" this week
with musical guest SZA?

00:05:25.567 --> 00:05:28.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Well...

00:05:28.567 --> 00:05:30.701
You just did.

00:05:30.701 --> 00:05:32.000
-Yeah, but you didn't.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.033
-Oh, sure.

00:05:33.033 --> 00:05:34.701
Keke Palmer is hosting "SNL"

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.968
this week with
musical guest SZA!

00:05:36.968 --> 00:05:38.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:38.734 --> 00:05:40.300
-Thanks, Jimmy.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:42.200
I knew we were friends.
-Yeah, we are best friends.

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:43.601
-Bye, guys.
-That's Keke Palmer right there.

00:05:43.601 --> 00:05:44.734
This weekend.
I'm rooting for you.

00:05:44.734 --> 00:05:45.801
Break a leg.
♪♪

00:05:50.133 --> 00:05:51.801
Guys -- Oh,
she's going to crush it.

00:05:51.801 --> 00:05:53.067
Guys, listen to this.

00:05:53.067 --> 00:05:55.634
According to new research,
self-service checkouts

00:05:55.634 --> 00:05:58.767
at grocery stores are
covered in harmful bacteria.

00:05:58.767 --> 00:06:04.033
But, hey, at least
they also never work.

00:06:04.033 --> 00:06:06.234
I love that, two years ago, we
were wiping down every surface,

00:06:06.234 --> 00:06:07.434
and now we're like,

00:06:07.434 --> 00:06:10.701
"Eh, my immune system
needs the challenge."

00:06:10.701 --> 00:06:12.934
Also, I read that researchers
in Europe developed a robot

00:06:12.934 --> 00:06:16.834
that braces itself
against walls to avoid falling.

00:06:19.868 --> 00:06:22.501
The robot's also programmed
to say, "I don't have a problem.

00:06:22.501 --> 00:06:24.534
You have a problem."

00:06:27.467 --> 00:06:29.734
Too bad they don't have
that for humans.

00:06:29.734 --> 00:06:31.734
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:35.567 --> 00:06:37.701
-What?!
-What?!

00:06:38.901 --> 00:06:40.601
What?!

00:06:41.801 --> 00:06:43.167
We have to see it again.
Can we see that one more time?

00:06:43.167 --> 00:06:44.300
It's just too funny.

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:46.300
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:50.801 --> 00:06:53.934
-Oh!
-Oh, my God.

00:06:53.934 --> 00:06:55.100
-Well, this is cool.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:57.033
I saw that the new
"Addams Family" series,

00:06:57.033 --> 00:06:58.968
"Wednesday," just passed
"Stranger Things"

00:06:58.968 --> 00:07:01.801
for most hours viewed
in a week on Netflix.

00:07:01.801 --> 00:07:04.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:07:04.801 --> 00:07:06.501
Tariq, are you
watching "Wednesday"?

00:07:06.501 --> 00:07:07.934
-Watching what Wednesday?

00:07:07.934 --> 00:07:09.734
-"Wednesday."

00:07:09.734 --> 00:07:12.234
-Yeah.
What are you watching Wednesday?

00:07:12.234 --> 00:07:13.567
-No, it's called "Wednesday."

00:07:13.567 --> 00:07:14.567
You can watch whenever --

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:16.334
Monday, Tuesday,
Wednesday, Thursday.

00:07:16.334 --> 00:07:18.367
-Are those other shows?

00:07:18.367 --> 00:07:21.434
-No, just "Wednesday."
I'm a "Wednesday" watcher.

00:07:21.434 --> 00:07:23.200
-Oh, I love "The Watcher."

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:24.667
I watched it Wednesday.

00:07:24.667 --> 00:07:28.200
-You watch "The Watcher" on
Wednesday, but not "Wednesday"?

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:30.534
-No, no, you can watch
"The Watcher" whenever you want,

00:07:30.534 --> 00:07:31.567
even Wednesday.

00:07:31.567 --> 00:07:34.400
Just watch "The Watcher,"
not "Wednesday."

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:36.767
-So you watched "The Watcher,"
not "Wednesday," on Wednesday

00:07:36.767 --> 00:07:38.634
while I was watching
"Wednesday" on Wednesday

00:07:38.634 --> 00:07:39.934
and not "The Watcher"?

00:07:39.934 --> 00:07:41.968
-That's the first thing
you've said that made

00:07:41.968 --> 00:07:43.000
any sense tonight.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:44.300
-Oh, Tariq Trotter, everyone.

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:45.801
Thank you very much. That's --

00:07:45.801 --> 00:07:47.601
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:51.434 --> 00:07:54.133
Well, last night was the
Rockefeller Center tree lighting

00:07:54.133 --> 00:07:55.601
here in New York,
but it was also

00:07:55.601 --> 00:07:58.000
the national tree lighting
in D.C.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:00.667
That's right --
two Christmas-tree lightings.

00:08:00.667 --> 00:08:03.634
Yeah. The national tree lighting
will be broadcast by CBS

00:08:03.634 --> 00:08:04.868
in two weeks.

00:08:04.868 --> 00:08:06.467
And I feel like
they're a little competitive,

00:08:06.467 --> 00:08:08.400
because here's the promo
they just released.

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:09.968
-Season's greetings, America.

00:08:09.968 --> 00:08:12.000
Are you tired of
lame Christmas tree lightings

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:13.267
at Rockefeller Center?

00:08:13.267 --> 00:08:14.767
Well [bleep] that [bleep]

00:08:14.767 --> 00:08:17.334
because the National Christmas
Tree Lighting is where it's at!

00:08:17.334 --> 00:08:19.701
We've got everything --
colorful lights, this star,

00:08:19.701 --> 00:08:21.534
a DJ named Splashy Dan!

00:08:21.534 --> 00:08:23.534
Rock Center's got
a cute, little squirrel.

00:08:23.534 --> 00:08:25.667
-Loser!
-But we got Cocaine Bear!

00:08:25.667 --> 00:08:27.534
[ Bear roars ]
And cocaine squirrel!

00:08:27.534 --> 00:08:30.033
And you think DJ Dan's
not on cocaine?

00:08:30.033 --> 00:08:32.667
He's on three drugs
you haven't even heard of!

00:08:32.667 --> 00:08:34.000
I hope you like ornaments,

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:36.601
because this Christmas tree's
got balls to the wall!

00:08:36.601 --> 00:08:39.434
So, this holiday season,
suck it, Rockefeller Center!

00:08:39.434 --> 00:08:42.067
Come watch a
real Christmas tree get lit!

00:08:44.834 --> 00:08:46.467
Ho-ho!

00:08:46.467 --> 00:08:49.200
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Wow!

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:51.400
Wow!

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:54.000
That is competitive.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:56.534
"It's Chrishmash, bish?"
-I have no idea.

00:08:56.534 --> 00:08:57.934
What are they
doing over there at CBS?

00:08:57.934 --> 00:09:00.968
-What do they do at CBS?
-Oh, my gosh.

00:09:02.934 --> 00:09:04.934
Finally, we have
exactly 12 shows left

00:09:04.934 --> 00:09:06.534
before we go on Christmas break.

00:09:06.534 --> 00:09:07.934
Yeah, that's right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:07.934 --> 00:09:09.334
Which means it's time for
that beloved

00:09:09.334 --> 00:09:10.501
"Tonight Show" tradition.

00:09:10.501 --> 00:09:14.467
It's time for "12 Days of
Christmas Sweaters"!

00:09:14.467 --> 00:09:16.968
-♪ "12 Days of
Christmas Sweaters ♪

00:09:16.968 --> 00:09:20.634
♪ 12 days left ♪

00:09:20.634 --> 00:09:21.701
-That's right.

00:09:21.701 --> 00:09:23.834
Every show between
now and Christmas,

00:09:23.834 --> 00:09:25.801
we'll be giving
one lucky audience member

00:09:25.801 --> 00:09:27.868
an out-of-this-world
Christmas sweater

00:09:27.868 --> 00:09:29.701
from the Countdown to
Christmas Cabinet.

00:09:29.701 --> 00:09:31.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:31.167 --> 00:09:36.834
Since there are 12 shows left,
let's open door number 12.

00:09:36.834 --> 00:09:38.133
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:09:38.133 --> 00:09:39.300
Hello.
-Hello.

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:41.901
-Nice to meet you.
-Nice to meet you, too.

00:09:45.501 --> 00:09:49.434
-Oh!
♪♪

00:09:49.434 --> 00:09:51.234
It's a sweater.

00:09:52.334 --> 00:09:54.734
Oh, my goodness.
This is like a...

00:09:54.734 --> 00:09:57.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:57.300 --> 00:09:59.868
Got mittens.

00:09:59.868 --> 00:10:01.901
It's got mittens there.
This is gorgeous.

00:10:01.901 --> 00:10:03.200
It's a Christmas sweater.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:05.901
Now let's see who's going
home with tonight's sweater.

00:10:05.901 --> 00:10:07.901
Everyone look at
your seat number.

00:10:07.901 --> 00:10:10.434
If I call your number,
come on down.

00:10:10.434 --> 00:10:12.200
Quest, can I get
a drumroll, please?

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:14.133
[ Drumroll ]

00:10:14.133 --> 00:10:16.567
Who wants a sweater?!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:18.434 --> 00:10:21.200
It is 211!
♪♪

00:10:23.767 --> 00:10:25.801
Come on over, bud. Hey.

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:30.534
How you doing, bud?

00:10:30.534 --> 00:10:33.467
Nice to see you.
Why don't you head over there.

00:10:33.467 --> 00:10:35.601
Yeah, go over there.
Nice to see you.

00:10:35.601 --> 00:10:37.000
How are you? What is your name?

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:38.434
-Mike.
-Mike, where are you from?

00:10:38.434 --> 00:10:39.868
-New York.
-Mike from New York. I love it.

00:10:39.868 --> 00:10:41.667
-Whoo!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:43.133 --> 00:10:45.634
I like your sweatshirt.

00:10:45.634 --> 00:10:48.267
Is that just a politeness
or is that a weed reference?

00:10:48.267 --> 00:10:49.901
-A little bit of --
A little bit of both.

